{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The War Within feels like a natural next choice because its intense thrash riffs connect with what draws me to Advance And Vanquish.",
    "The End of Heartache and This Darkened Heart combine heavy guitar work with melody, which fits my interest in Colony, Figure Number Five and other In Flames albums."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Long Road connects with my accessible rock listening, but it misses my current desire for heavier, more aggressive music.",
    "Sevendust, Seasons and Lost and Found fit parts of my taste, but their appeal is less immediate than the metal albums I would choose today; saving them for later does not mean I dislike them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My history of listening to accessible rock seems to carry too much weight when I am currently choosing heavier music.",
    "Heavy riffs alone do not make every album equally appealing to me; I care about the particular combination of intensity, melody and guitar work."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in Advance And Vanquish makes the forceful thrash sound of The War Within especially compelling.",
    "I would only choose a few albums now, so passing over an appealing album can reflect my priorities today rather than a poor match."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations mostly understand my taste for melodic, aggressive music, but give accessible heavy rock more priority than I want today."
}"}
